{
  "case_id": "2009-09-559",
  "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:11 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (James Bopp, Jr., Esq.)",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No person should suffer harassment for participating in our political system, and the First Amendment protects citizens from intimidation resulting from compelled disclosure of their identity and beliefs and their private associations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What -- what about requiring disclosure of campaign contributions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0000-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has upheld the disclosure in Buckley v. Valeo in 1976."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I\u2019m -- I'm trying to separate out the harassment aspects of this case from the working proposition that there\u2019s some sort of freedom of association, of privacy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (James Bopp, Jr., Esq.)",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BOPP: Well, we\u2019re only challenging the application of the Public Records Act to petitions and referendum petitions. We're not challenging it as it would be applied to petitions to put people on the ballot."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BOPP",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Washington provides no way for the public, even if they get access to the petitions, to participate in the verification process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. BOPP",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What I -- what I said is there\u2019s no role for the public in verifying signatures. You can ask for judicial review --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why would they ask for judicial review instead of going first to the State's Attorney General and saying, look, you -- your people missed it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. McKENNA",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I\u2019d like to begin with the question of how the public can bring to the attention of the government that errors and fraud have been discovered."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. McKENNA",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they can obtain records --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Would it be consistent with the First Amendment to require anybody who signs a petition to list the person's religion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, of course -- yes, they could apply for another preliminary injunction if this Court upholds the court of appeals. They were able to obtain that preliminary injunction in this case, which is why these petition forms have not been released to date, except under a protective order by the court to the opponents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is that because nobody got to count 2? And the district court -- this whole case in the lower courts was on count 1 alone; wasn't that so?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, let's say somebody is thinking of circulating a petition on a sensitive subject and fears that people may be dissuaded from signing because they fear retaliation. At what point could they bring this as-applied challenge?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's the fraud interest."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0003-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "this Court upheld the requirement by Colorado that affidavits signed by the petition circulators, including the petition circulator's name and address, can be disclosed as public records."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Petitioners have stressed that Buckley II struck down the requirement to wear the name badge."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: You know, if somebody called your office and said I'd like the -- the home address of all the attorneys who work in the Attorney General\u2019s Office because we want to -- we want to go to their homes and have uncomfortable conversations with them -- (Laughter.) JUSTICE ALITO: -- which is what has been alleged here, would you release that information?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Third, evidence of harassment comes in, as in Citizens United, because the weight of the interest that is required depends upon the burden of the First Amendment -- to the First Amendment speech involved; and this Court specifically referred in Citizens United to the lack of evidence of harassment of the donors that might occur if they were disclosed through the reports which Citizens United upheld. Here we do have evidence of harassment, and we believe that that requires a greater burden in the First Amendment analysis --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96c1dcdfa12180fd3b05dfc99be26c310aa28c5c4daae97ff7bfd823138ed7fe",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96c1dcdfa121-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: The court did not rule on whether there was a risk of harassment here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-09-559",
      "confidence": 0.0,
